1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,800
Deep in the pitch-black void between stars, something massive is moving.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:10,500
We grow up learning that planets orbit stars. But what if trillions of worlds are completely alone?

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:19,500
Billions of years ago, chaotic planetary nurseries played gravitational billiards, hurling newborn worlds forever out into the icy interstellar dark.

4
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:34,500
Without a sun, their skies freeze to minus two hundred degrees. But peel back miles of nitrogen ice, and radioactive cores keep colossal liquid oceans churning in total darkness.

5
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:46,500
Powered by geothermal vents, warm abyssal seas could harbor bizarre bioluminescent ecosystems, drifting through the galaxy as self-contained cosmic arks.

6
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:56,500
In fact, rogue planets may outnumber all stars in the Milky Way. Dark, invisible wanderers, quietly filling the void.

7
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,600
The universe isn't empty. It's waiting.

